# Golden fixture corpora are checksum-pinned (see
# backend/app/modules/calculation/golden_manifest.py): their exact bytes are
# the contract that manifest.json's sha256 checks on every test run. Line
# ending normalization on checkout must never touch them — confirmed on this
# Windows machine (core.autocrlf=true) turning an LF-committed corpus.json
# into CRLF on checkout, which then failed its own recorded checksum despite
# the JSON content being byte-for-byte unchanged otherwise.
backend/app/modules/calculation/specs/**/golden/**/*.json -text
